{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QBesselContiguityRecurrence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBesselContiguityRecurrence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.lever1_habiro_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.lever1_habiro_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L171-L184","doc":"**Lever-1 Kernel Product Form (CONDITIONAL).**\n*If* a sequence `D` satisfies the Hahn-Exton q-Bessel recurrence `hrec` for some `(q, a)`,\n*then* it has the q-Bessel product form. This is a sound conditional alias of\n`qbessel_coeff_closed_form`; it does NOT assert that the binding correction `D(m)`\nsatisfies `hrec` (it does not — held-out falsified, see `lever1HabiroRatio` scope note).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.lever1HabiroRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.lever1HabiroRatio","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L149-L169","doc":"**Lever-1 Fibre Kernel — Hahn-Exton contiguity ratio (shared Habiro-ring class).**\nThe correction to the binding period `S(m)` relative to the order-2 q-involution\nskeleton is the cyclotomic Habiro sequence `D(m)`. This alias names the Hahn-Exton\nq-Bessel ratio `qbesselRatio` for use in the conditional product form below.\n\nSCOPE (per `docs/audits/2026-06-28-lever1-binding-correction-not-single-qhypergeometric.md`):\n`D(m)` shares the *Hahn-Exton / Habiro-ring class* with the Q_β `c_k` ladder — both\nare cyclotomic-completion objects with `ζ₄` residues — but this is a shared-CLASS\nanalogy, NOT a literal contiguity identity. `D(m)` does **not** satisfy the\nsingle-parameter Hahn-Exton recurrence: the literal contiguity template was tested\nwith held-out-`m` falsification and FAILS (no single `a` fit on `m=4,5` predicts\n`m=6,7,8`), and `D(m)` factors as a product of pairwise-coprime irreducible\nbar-symmetric cores of growing degree (Stages 7-9), not a single q-hypergeometric\nelement. The bare Hahn-Exton ratio is likewise structurally excluded for the parallel\n`c_k` (2026-06-20 audit, `r₂ = +2` in the forbidden gap). So `lever1HabiroRatio` is\nthe q-Bessel ratio re-exported as the class representative, not a claim that `D(m)` is\ngoverned by it.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qbessel_second_kind_coeff_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qbessel_second_kind_coeff_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L139-L147","doc":"**Jackson's Second Kind q-Bessel contiguity.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qbesselSecondKindRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qbesselSecondKindRatio","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L132-L137","doc":"**Jackson's Second Kind q-Bessel coefficient ratio.**\nAlso associated with `SU_q(1,1)`, its ratio is\n`r_k = -a q^{2k+1} / [(1-q^{k+1})(1-a q^{k+1})]` (with `a = q^ν`).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qbessel_first_kind_coeff_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qbessel_first_kind_coeff_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L122-L130","doc":"**Jackson's First Kind q-Bessel contiguity.** ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:jackson-q-bessel-contiguity-recurrence","label":"prop:jackson-q-bessel-contiguity-recurrence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jackson-q-bessel-contiguity-recurrence.md"},{"@id":"block:prf:jackson-q-bessel-contiguity","label":"prf:jackson-q-bessel-contiguity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jackson-q-bessel-contiguity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qbesselFirstKindRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qbesselFirstKindRatio","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L115-L120","doc":"**Jackson's First Kind q-Bessel coefficient ratio.**\nAssociated with the quantum hyperbolic plane `SU_q(1,1)`, its ratio is\n`r_k = -1 / [(1-q^{k+1})(1-a q^{k+1})]` (with `a = q^ν`).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qbessel_second_order_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qbessel_second_order_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L98-L113","doc":"**Second-order q-difference equation `☆`, coefficient form.** The Hahn–Exton\nq-Bessel generating function `g(w) = Σ c_k w^k` satisfies\n`q^ν·g(q²w) − (1+q^ν−w)·g(qw) + g(w) = 0` (the function-level q-Bessel equation;\nverified to 60 dps in\n`computations/qbeta/qbessel_second_order_qdifference_equation.py`).\nIts `w^{k+1}` coefficient is the relation below, which follows from the\nfirst-order `★` via `qbessel_second_order_factor`. The \"second order\" is the\nq-difference order (three q-shifts `w, qw, q²w`); on the coefficients it collapses\nto the consecutive-`c_k` relation, so this and `★` are equivalent. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:q-bessel-second-order-qdifference","label":"prf:q-bessel-second-order-qdifference","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-bessel-second-order-qdifference.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qbessel_second_order_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qbessel_second_order_factor","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L88-L96","doc":"**Factorisation behind the second-order q-difference equation `☆`.** The\nmiddle coefficient of the q-Bessel q-difference equation factors into the `★`\ndenominator: with `a = q^{ν+1}` (so `q^ν · q = a`),\n`a·q^{2k+1} − q^{k+1} − a·q^k + 1 = (1 − q^{k+1})(1 − a·q^k)`. This is the purely\nalgebraic reason the *second-order* operator reduces to the *first-order* (★). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.geometric_of_constant_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.geometric_of_constant_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L76-L86","doc":"**C-finite degeneration.** When the ratio is a *constant* `ρ` (the rational /\n`q → 1` limit), the sequence is geometric `c_k = c_0 · ρ^k` — C-finite of order 1\nwith characteristic root `ρ`. The genuine q-Bessel case has the `q^k`-dependent\nratio `qbesselRatio` above and is therefore NOT of this form: it is q-holonomic,\nwhich is why the canonical `c_k` admit no low-order constant-coefficient\nrecurrence (#1839). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qbessel_coeff_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qbessel_coeff_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L64-L74","doc":"**q-Bessel contiguity ⟹ closed-form coefficients (q-holonomic).** From the\nfirst-order q-recurrence (★) and the non-degeneracy of its denominators, the\ncoefficients are the q-hypergeometric product `c_k = c_0 · ∏_{j<k} r_j`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:q-bessel-c-k-recurrence-cfinite","label":"prf:q-bessel-c-k-recurrence-cfinite","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-bessel-c-k-recurrence-cfinite.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qbesselRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qbesselRatio","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The Hahn–Exton q-Bessel coefficient ratio `r_k = −q^k / [(1−q^{k+1})(1−a q^k)]`\n(with `a = q^{ν+1}`). The `q^k`-dependence is what makes the `c_k` q-holonomic\nrather than C-finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.first_order_solution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.first_order_solution","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean#L49-L56","doc":"**First-order linear recurrence ⟹ product solution.** If `c_{k+1} = r_k · c_k`\nfor all `k`, then `c_k = c_0 · ∏_{j<k} r_j`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}